  "verdict": "ACCEPT_BOUNDED_EXISTING_SOURCE_RECONCILIATION_DESIGN",
  "basis": [
    "The original donor full-release contract and current shared partial/native contracts exist at their proper owner; integrate their useful behavior instead of creating another comparator or service",
    "Explicit inventory-only export preserves old capability; breaking default full admission receives original semantic release selection, current partial source publication does not wait for installation",
    "Full admission composes the two existing admitted comparisons and binds the same archive/release identity; successful pure comparisons state supplied-facts scope and cannot authorize native effects",
    "SHA256 correction repairs the original primitive already-declared full40/64 OID contract through native explicit storage format; no duplicate Git codec or Networking dependency",
    "A differently serialized publisher remains a genuine selected-supplier precondition; no arbitrary expected-manifest JSON waiver or fabricated alternate producer is admitted"
  ],
  "conditions": [
    "Classify source changes under existing-source recovery/maintenance; new behavior or supplier beyond these selected original contracts returns to the current CbC native fabrication gate",
    "Use exact source-owner isolated proposal; preserve all unique PR15 authority/factory work and occupied versions; independently receive source proposal before integration",
    "Retain zero-dependency primitive public API and identity forwarding. Receive its actual qualified publication before updating Code normal manifest/lock; reconcile real Git forwarding consumer when its supported SHA256 input needs that provider",
    "Qualify exact native Git init/object-format/fetch signatures before effect and use actual native SHA1/SHA256 repositories through existing reader and actual released CLI",
    "Predeclared full/partial/native-mode/nonmutation/refusal regressions and full owner suite must pass; a failed assay returns to disputed contract, not trial patches",
    "Do not mutate current common runtime/lock or upgrade GHS solely for a version label; select each actual caller only when its original receiving condition requires it",
    "No new deployment, installer, publisher, source reader, receipt authority, workspace prerequisite or arbitrary serialization acceptance"
  ],
  "notClaimed": [
    "constructed source or source-free native fabrication",
    "new tests executed",
    "full-v2 or SHA256 product received",
    "PR24 complete or superseded",
    "live GHS/machine uptake"
  ],
